<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Notes for users of Cyrillic languages>

  To type Russian or another Cyrillic language, configure the corresponding
  keyboard layout or input method in the operating system and enter text
  normally. ATHENA accepts the resulting Unicode text directly and does not
  provide an application-specific Cyrillic input method.

  The language controls in ATHENA describe the document content for
  typesetting and language-sensitive features; they do not remap physical
  keyboard keys. Select Russian for an entire document using
  <menu|Document|Language|Russian>, or for a portion of text using
  <menu|Format|Language|Russian>.

